//! Phosphor's icons, as the path data it publishes.
//!
//! Each string is the `d` of the one `<path>` in an SVG of
//! `@phosphor-icons/core` 2.1.1, bold weight, copied byte for byte so a
//! line can be checked against phosphoricons.com. Named as Phosphor names
//! them, with `_` for `-`. `icons.zig` says what fenrir draws each one for.
//!
//! Path data rather than Phosphor's font, because it is what starts fastest:
//! the 29 icons here parse in 74us, where `Phosphor-Bold.ttf` takes 150us to
//! read before its first glyph is decoded. And they are not even parsed at
//! startup: `icons.zig` has the compiler do that.
//!
//! On a 256-unit grid with y down, filled, holes wound against their outer
//! contour for the nonzero rule.
